  "body": "It is useful for web authors do determine when their `<dialog>` elements open and close. `popover` already has `ToggleEvent` which is dispatched when a `popover` opens or closes, but `<dialog>` does not. The current way to detect when a `<dialog>` opens is to register a mutation observer to check for `open`, however, this is quite a lot of work where an event would be easier.\r\n\r\nI propose we add dispatching of `ToggleEvent` for `<dialog>` also. To be explicit: when `showModal` is called, `<dialog>` should dispatch a `ToggleEvent` with `newState=open`. When a dialog is closed (via form or button or close signal) it should dispatch a `ToggleEvent` with `newState=closed`.\r\n\r\n[Spec PR](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10091)",
